.TH SWAYDESK-CLIP-STORE 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.2.0" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-clip\-store \- store non\-text clipboard content in cliphist
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-clip\-store
.SH DESCRIPTION
Not meant to be run directly: the Sway configuration runs it under wl\-paste \-\-watch, with no type. It reads the copied content on standard input and stores it with cliphist store when it is neither text nor an image (a PDF, a file copied as bytes), since text and images have their own watchers. Above 5 MB it does not store anything.
.PP
The session runs it under the name sway\-clip\-store (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-clip\-store); the process name is sway\-clip\-store too.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLIPBOARD_STATE
Set by wl\-paste; anything other than data (sensitive, clear) is left to the text watcher.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cliphist (1),
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR swaydesk\-clipboard\-popup (1),
.BR wl\-paste (1)
